kunzite: Adreno 710 step 16, the GMU's RPMh channel and HFI start (kgpu=16; 1-15 unchanged).
16 continues kgsl's gen7_gmu_first_boot after gen7_gmu_device_start, the GMU running as step 15
left it (FW_INIT_RESULT 0x100, CM3 out of reset; checked first). gen7_load_rsc_ucode into the
RSCC (0x3d50000), in kgsl's order: STATUS0 bit 24 (SDE clock gating off), PDC_SLAVE_ID 1, the
three hidden TCS commands (0, 0, data 0x80000000: gen7_3_0 is not in the gen7_2_x family),
OVERRIDE_START_ADDR 0, PDC_SEQ_START_ADDR 0x4520, PDC_MATCH_VALUE 0x4510/0x4514, and the five
sequencer words at SEQ_MEM_0 (0x180); every word read back. gen7_load_pdc_ucode into the GPU PDC
(0xb270000): SEQ_START_ADDR 0, ENABLE_PDC 0x80000001 (the boot leaves 0x101). kgsl writes these
once per boot and never takes them back; here all 19 are undone at the end (the boot's words
back, popped before step 15's reset, the GMU idle in its HFI loop). Then gen7_gmu_hfi_start:
HFI_CTRL_INIT 1 (kept) and HFI_CTRL_STATUS bit 0 polled for 100 ms (boot #36 already saw 1
right after the firmware started, so the before/after values are printed), 100 ms more, then
GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO decoded (msgq, dbgq, CM3 fault, OOB), the log's non-zero words before and
after, the three queue headers and the debug queue's first words if it has any, CB1 FSR. No HFI
message is sent (step 17). The log count now covers the whole 64K log (step 15 too, through a
helper); KG_UNDO_MAX 40 -> 64 (the undo peaks at 39).

